---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/use-cases/product-launch';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/product-launch');
const desc = description(site, 'use-cases/product-launch');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does a waitlist reserve inventory?",
    "answer": "Only if the stated policy and purchase system actually reserve it. Signup alone should not promise a unit."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can email arrival establish a fair queue?",
    "answer": "No. Enforce allocation in the purchase system and communicate the policy explicitly."
  },
  {
    "question": "Must zero-stock products leave launch emails?",
    "answer": "Check the approved sales policy; intentional preorders need accurate availability and fulfillment wording."
  },
  {
    "question": "What happens after a buyer purchases?",
    "answer": "Exit remaining sales reminders for that item and hand off to the appropriate post-purchase path."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <article class="container prose-shopify py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">All use cases</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Shopify product launch email: access, allocation and availability</h1>
    <p>Coordinate the launch promise with the purchase path. A waitlist, an access window and reserved stock are different commitments; the email must say which one the buyer actually has.</p>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>Publish an access contract</h2>
      <p>Define the product and variants, eligible audience, release time and timezone, purchase limits and fulfillment promise. Decide whether access is public, gated or allocated. An early email alone does not prevent its link being shared, and send order cannot guarantee inbox arrival order.</p>
      <p>If signup order determines allocation, enforce that policy in the purchase or reservation system. Do not call a waitlist a reservation unless inventory is actually held. Tell subscribers what happens if their preferred variant is unavailable and whether they must request future notifications separately.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>Match the launch to inventory policy</h2>
      <p>Shopify supports continuing to sell an out-of-stock product or variant when configured. Therefore zero stock does not by itself tell the email team whether to stop: the item may intentionally be a preorder. Have merchandising approve whether each variant is ready to ship, preorder, backorder or unavailable.</p>
      <p>Record the authoritative stock source, its update delay and a person who can pause remaining sends. Recheck eligibility and purchase status before each wave. An inventory check cannot recall an already-delivered email, so the landing page must explain current availability and any changed fulfillment expectation.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>Coordinate audiences and offers</h2>
      <p>Define how VIP access, waitlist access and public release relate. A person can qualify for several audiences; resolve that overlap once and remove buyers from remaining sales reminders. Recent purchasers may still want an expansion or compatible accessory, so blanket recent-buyer exclusion is not always useful.</p>
      <p>Align cart recovery and welcome incentives with the launch offer. Publish the actual redemption terms and have checkout enforce them. Use SMS only for the appropriately subscribed audience with a distinct purpose, rather than duplicating the same launch announcement automatically across every channel.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>Prepare for an interrupted launch</h2>
      <p>Write a factual fallback for a delayed release, broken checkout or cancelled allocation. A pause should stop queued promotional waves as well as the next scheduled campaign. Update the product page and support brief together so subscribers do not receive contradictory explanations.</p>
      <p>Coordinate press and creator links with the access promise. If a public link is expected to work before the waitlist email, say so in the launch plan. After sellout, offer a relevant notification choice rather than claiming new stock is certain. Purchased items hand off to fulfillment and education instead of another last-chance message.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>A proposed limited-edition rehearsal</h2>
      <p>For a board-game release, model a buyer eligible for VIP and waitlist access, another requesting only one variant, and a third buying before the public wave. Change a variant from available to preorder during the rehearsal. Inspect access enforcement, page wording, recipient deduplication and remaining queued messages. This is a proposed exercise, not an observed launch.</p>
      <p>Evaluate Sequenzy or another candidate against that same sequence rather than accepting a launch-template demo. Ask who owns allocation enforcement and what happens when stock sync fails. Report sales by audience using non-overlapping definitions, with cancellations, fulfillment delays and unmet notification requests alongside revenue. Attributed launch revenue alone does not prove incremental demand.</p>
    </section>
    <p>Primary reference checked November 25, 2026: <a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/inventory-and-locations/setup/selling-when-out-of-stock">Shopify out-of-stock sales settings</a>. Workflow recommendations and proposed checks above are editorial guidance, not claims of completed testing.</p>
    <p>Continue with <a class="link" href="/use-cases/back-in-stock">back in stock</a>, <a class="link" href="/use-cases/post-purchase">post purchase</a>. Browse the <a class="link" href="/apps">tool catalog</a> for candidates; confirm current capabilities and costs for the required integration.</p>
  </article>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Product launch FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
